{
  "about": [
    "The limits GOAT Style takes from MapLibre, by GOAT setting. goatlib's models read them through goatlib.style.limits;",
    "apps/web/lib/style/__tests__/maplibre-limits.test.ts fails when the installed MapLibre style spec no longer matches.",
    "models: the model fields (Model.field in the JSON Schema; * matches any name; Zoom*.zoom.0 is a zoom stop's zoom).",
    "maplibre: what the setting compiles to, as <spec group>.<name>; a value drawn into an image names the image property.",
    "spec: copied from MapLibre's style spec, over all of maplibre: the highest minimum, the lowest maximum, for paint and",
    "layout properties the zoom expressions they take (blend: interpolated, step, null: none) and whether they take",
    "data-driven ones (feature).",
    "goat: where goatlib sets its own value instead: min, max, zoom, attribute (attribute mappings; default: feature) and",
    "per_feature (classes and rules may set it; default: feature) and choice (a name the compiler turns into the value:",
    "MapLibre's min and max bound what the compiler writes, not the name). Everything else is spec's.",
    "differs: why goatlib allows more than MapLibre for this setting."
  ],
